---
layout: base.njk
permalink: "/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ site.name }} — storage with published access hours, climate control, and month-to-month terms"
  description: "{{ site.description }}"
  breadcrumbs:
    - name: Home
      url: /
---
<section class="page-hero wrap">
  {% include "partials/breadcrumbs.njk" %}
  <p class="eyebrow">A public-source directory</p>
  <h1>{{ site.tagline }}</h1>
  <p class="lede">{{ site.description }} We only list hours and amenity flags that a facility publishes, and we date every check. If we cannot verify it, it does not go on the page. We do not cache live unit prices or vacancy — if a price appears, it is labeled as listed on a date.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap" id="cities">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Cities</h2>
    <p class="muted">Each city is one data file, so a new page can ship as soon as the listings are verified.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="city-grid">
    {% for city in cities %}
    <li>
      <a class="city-card" href="{{ city | cityPath }}">
        <h3>{{ city.city }}, {{ city.state }}</h3>
        <p>{% if city.focus %}{{ city.focus }} focus · {% endif %}{{ city.listings | length }} listings</p>
        <p class="small muted">Updated {{ city.lastUpdated | displayDate }}</p>
      </a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap tonight">
  <h2>Why this directory exists</h2>
  <p>People looking for storage often need a unit they can reach after work, climate control for furniture or documents, and a lease they can end month to month. Generic “storage near me” lists rarely separate gate hours from office hours, and a “24/7” badge on a marketing page is not always the same as published around-the-clock access.</p>
  <p><a href="/guides/need-storage-access-at-night-how-24-hour-storage-really-works/">Read the night-access guide</a> · <a href="/about/">How we research listings</a></p>
</section>
